  data:  # 76f3
    kind: work_item  # 76f3
    title: "ipc linker: a main-process handler registered through a custom wrapper (podman-desktop this.ipcHandle('ch', ...)) is no receive site, so 65 of 66 podman contextBridge callers still stop at the preload"  # 76f3
    status: todo_hard  # 76f3
    priority: 2  # 76f3
    parent:  # 76f3
    tags:  # 76f3
    - analysis_quality  # 76f3
    isbefore: []  # 76f3
    duplicate_of: []  # 76f3
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 76f3
    pr_ref:  # 76f3
    description: "Found during WI-kokuv-dakak-sitop-tinul-jodin-gizoh-namir-dakum (branch jgstern-agent/fix/kokuv, 098155b5a0). linkers/ipc.py detects receivers only via ipcMain.on/.handle/.handleOnce and ipcRenderer.on/.once. A main process that registers handlers through its own wrapper, e.g. podman-desktop packages/main/src/plugin/index.ts:280 `ipcHandle(channel, listener)` called as `this.ipcHandle('containerfile:getInfo', ...)` (containerfile-parser.ts:34, index.ts:472, and many more), yields NO receive site for those channels. Effect, measured with link_ipc on ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/podman-desktop/packages after the kokuv fix: 66 contextBridge bridge callers, 58 distinct preload send nodes, and only 1 bridge caller reaches any ipcMain receiver, so the renderer -> preload -> main chain still stops at the preload for 65 of 66 callers. The send side already accepts custom wrappers (ipcInvoke/ipcSend in _FUNC_BODY_IPC_PATTERN, and the kokuv fix lets those wrapper send sites join receivers); the receive side has no such path. Likely shape of a fix: detect a same-repo function/method whose body forwards its first parameter to ipcMain.handle/on (`ipcMain.handle(channel, ...)`) and treat literal-channel calls to that function as receive sites. That is the same wrapper-forwarding mechanism as the send-side ipcInvoke support, mirrored. Corpus impact beyond podman-desktop: not measured."  # 76f3
    fields: {}  # 76f3
- op: discuss  # 5f12
  at: '2026-11-01T04:01:41Z'  # 5f12
  by: agent  # 5f12
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5f12
  clock: 2  # 5f12
  nonce: 5f12  # 5f12
  message: "Fix on branch jgstern-agent/fix/pumit, commit 1bcda5de6f (not merged). Premise reproduced on a fixture: the bridge caller reached no receiver, and there was one param->param variable_match edge. The send side had no real wrapper detection to share: it accepted ipcInvoke/ipcSend by NAME, and only inside contextBridge function exposures. The new mechanism serves both directions. One rule table (_ELECTRON_SITE_RULES) is read by both the site scan and the wrapper scan. A function or method that forwards its first parameter to any Electron IPC call is a wrapper. A literal or same-file-constant call that can see it is a site at the call line. The forwarding call itself is no site.\n\nScope is repo-wide by name, gated per call form:\n- bare f(): the wrapper is in the same file, or the file imports f.\n- this.f(): the call is inside the wrapper's class, or the file declares an f member (the DI shape).\n- x.f(): x is bound to new C() of the wrapper's class.\n\nAlso in the same file: ipcMain.once is now a receive site.\n\npodman-desktop/packages: bridge callers reaching main went from 1/66 to 66/66. event_publishes went from 32 to 322 (+302, -12). The 12 removed edges are all param->param variable_match. Max fan-out is 1. A random sample of 12 plus every non-index.ts edge was read against source, and all are correct.\n\nvscode: 24 spurious param/comment variable_match edges removed and 10 correct edges added (validatedIpcMain.handle/on, CodeWindow this.send, acquirePort).\n\nA full hypergumbo run on the fixture connects renderer bridge_caller -> preload send -> main receive, with every endpoint present as a node. This answers the kokuv path-format question for the fixture only.\n\nFiled: WI-pisur-mohaj-tisit-ninul-romok-gidad-ladop-lajob (sites detected inside comments). Not done: wrapper-of-wrapper (one level only); object-literal bridge methods calling a wrapper (_BRIDGE_METHOD_PATTERN; no corpus instance found)."  # 5f12
