- op: discuss  # d8b3
  at: '2026-11-01T07:56:28Z'  # d8b3
  by: agent  # d8b3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d8b3
  clock: 4  # d8b3
  nonce: d8b3  # d8b3
  message: "Fixed in PR #1985 (merged to dev 6afecacb1b). Root cause: linkers/ipc.py recognised only direct ipcRenderer/ipcMain calls as Electron IPC sites, so a project that routes IPC through its own wrapper (podman-desktop's `this.ipcHandle('ch', ...)`) had one site per wrapper (the forwarding call inside it, with a non-literal channel) and none at the real call sites. Fix: one _ELECTRON_SITE_RULES table; _ipc_wrappers finds same-repo functions/methods that forward their channel parameter to an Electron IPC call; _wrapper_call_sites makes each call of such a wrapper a site (with visibility rules); the forwarding call itself is dropped as a site; ipcMain.once added. 15 tests in test_ipc_wrapper_sites.py. Live repro on merged dev (fixture: renderer app.ts calls the bridge, preload exposes it, main registers through its own wrapper): `hypergumbo survey fx1` rc=0 -> renderer load() reaches ipc:packages/main/index.ts:9-9:receive:containerfile:getInfo; edges: event_publishes preload send:containerfile:getInfo -> main receive:containerfile:getInfo, and main PluginSystem.init uses that receive. Corpus (fix agent): podman-desktop 66 of 66 bridge calls reach a main-process receive, up from 1; vscode lost 24 false edges and gained 10 correct ones. Residuals: WI-pisur (IPC sites inside comments, P3), filed by the fix agent; evidence_types.py ipc_channel_match prose cites a stale ipc.py:546, filed separately."  # d8b3
